PART 2: UNDERSTANDING REACT COMPONENTS

================================================================================

What is a React Component?

A React component is typically a JavaScript function that returns/describes UI using JSX.

Component Feature       | Description
------------------------|-------------------------------------------
JavaScript Function     | Modern components are usually functions
JSX                     | Describes the component's UI
State                   | Component can use its own state
Props                   | Component can receive data/input
Logic                   | Component can contain UI-related logic
Reusable                | Can be used multiple times
Composable              | Components can contain other components

Component Analogy - LEGO Blocks

Think of components like LEGO blocks.

LEGO                         | React
-----------------------------|-------------------------------------
Individual block             | Individual component
Reusable block               | Reusable component
Combine multiple blocks      | Combine multiple components
Each block has a purpose     | Each component has a responsibility
Complex LEGO structure       | Complete React application


Easy memory:

SMALL COMPONENTS
      ↓
COMBINED TOGETHER
      ↓
LARGER COMPONENTS
      ↓
COMPLETE APPLICATION


================================================================================

TYPES OF COMPONENTS

================================================================================

React applications can contain functional components and older class components.

1. Functional Components - Modern Approach
function MyComponent() {
  return <h1>Hello World</h1>;
}


Characteristics:

Feature             | Functional Component
--------------------|--------------------------------
Definition          | JavaScript function
UI                  | Returns/describes JSX
State               | Can use Hooks such as useState
Modern React        | Commonly used
Readability         | Usually concise

2. Class Components - Older Style
class MyComponent extends React.Component {
  render() {
    return <h1>Hello World</h1>;
  }
}


Characteristics:

Feature             | Class Component
--------------------|---------------------------------
Definition          | JavaScript class
Base Class          | Extends React.Component
UI                  | Returned from render()
State               | Can use this.state
Style               | Older React code style
Support             | Still encountered in existing code

Functional vs Class Components
Feature         | Functional Component   | Class Component
----------------|------------------------|-----------------------
Structure       | JavaScript function    | JavaScript class
JSX             | Returned directly      | Returned by render()
State           | Hooks                  | this.state
State Update    | Hook state setter      | this.setState()
Modern Usage    | Common approach        | Older/legacy codebases
Boilerplate     | Usually less           | Usually more

Course Focus
THIS COURSE
     ↓
FUNCTIONAL COMPONENTS
     ↓
HOOKS
     ↓
MODERN REACT STYLE


