PART 4: COMPONENT NAMING CONVENTIONS

================================================================================

Rule 1: Use PascalCase

================================================================================

React component names should start with an uppercase letter.

Correct
function Welcome() {}

function UserProfile() {}

function TodoItem() {}

Avoid
function welcome() {}

function user_profile() {}

function todoitem() {}

Why PascalCase?
Example          | Meaning
-----------------|---------------------------------
<Welcome />      | React component
<UserProfile />  | React component
<TodoItem />     | React component
<div>            | Built-in HTML element
<button>         | Built-in HTML element


React JSX uses capitalization to distinguish user-defined React components from lowercase built-in HTML elements.

Easy memory:

Uppercase / PascalCase
→ React Component

Lowercase
→ HTML Element


================================================================================

Rule 2: Use Descriptive Names

================================================================================

Names should describe the component's responsibility.

Good Names
function UserCard() {}

function NavigationBar() {}

function LoginForm() {}

Less Descriptive Names
function Component() {}

function Item() {}

function Container() {}

Why Use Descriptive Names?
Benefit              | Explanation
---------------------|-----------------------------------------
Readability          | Purpose is immediately clearer
Self-documentation   | Name explains intended responsibility
Maintenance          | Easier to find and modify code
Team Collaboration   | Other developers understand intent faster


================================================================================

Rule 3: Match File Name and Component Name

================================================================================

A common React project convention is to keep the component filename aligned with the component name.

Recommended
File                  | Component
----------------------|-----------------------
Welcome.jsx           | Welcome
UserProfile.jsx       | UserProfile
TodoItem.jsx          | TodoItem
NavigationBar.jsx     | NavigationBar


Example:

// File: Welcome.jsx

export default function Welcome() {
  return <h1>Welcome</h1>;
}


Another example:

// File: UserProfile.jsx

export default function UserProfile() {
  return <div>User Profile</div>;
}

Avoid Inconsistent Naming
File          | Component       | Issue
--------------|-----------------|-----------------------------
welcome.jsx   | Welcome         | Inconsistent capitalization
user.jsx      | UserProfile     | File doesn't describe component

Why Match Them?
Welcome.jsx
    ↓
Welcome

UserProfile.jsx
    ↓
UserProfile


Benefits:

Easier file navigation.
Easier searching.
Clear component ownership.
Better project organization.
Easier team collaboration.

